[general] The data sample used for the analysis is internally unclear, especially below the GZK threshold.

**What is wrong:** Several different energy domains are invoked:
- the abstract says the relative fraction above \(10^{19}\) eV can be found;
- Sec. 3 and Fig. 3 describe “720 cosmic rays above the GZK limit,” with Fig. 3 titled \(>50\) EeV;
- Sec. 4 defines a pre-GZK baseline \(\Delta E_0=(30{-}50)\) EeV;
- Table 1 includes bins beginning at \((32{-}35)\) EeV, below the stated GZK scale \(5\times10^{19}\) eV \(=50\) EeV.

The manuscript does not explain whether the 720-event sample includes only \(>50\) EeV events, how the \(30{-}50\) EeV baseline data were obtained, or whether the same exposure treatment applies below and above 50 EeV.
